>
> Questions in round one are worth 5 points each.
> 1. This member of the ape-like creatures gives its name to the group
> symbol 'Y'.
Ape. (They are *ape-like*, after all.)
> 2. Fungi and jellies usually have what type of attack?
Passive.
> 3. Are the symbol for a soldier and the symbol for a priest the same?
Yes and no: without colour both are '@'; with colour the soldier is a
gray '@' and the priest is a white '@' (which can be considered a
different glyph).
> 4. This food abuses your wisdom and makes you nauseous.
No food both abuses your wisdom and makes you nauseous.  Search
the source for make_vomiting (which only appears in its normal context
in eat.c) and for "exercise(A_WIS, FALSE)" for abusing wisdom, which
does not appear in eat.c Are you thinking of tripe rations, which produce
the "Yak - dog food!" message if you're not an orc or a caveman but do
not abuse wisdom?
> 5. What is the 'special' spell for rangers?
Invisibility.
> 6. This is the other food that nauseates.
Several foods nauseate, though you're probably thinking of rotten eggs.
(Others include the aforementioned tripe ration, rotten tins, and, if
you're undead, a clove of garlic.)
> 7. As a Valkyrie, will you ever suddenly feel very cold?
No - you have natural cold resistance which can never be removed.
> 8. Name the colors that an 'L' might appear in.
Strictly speaking, they can appear in any colour due to hallucinogenic
effects.  But actual liches can appear in brown (lich), red (demilich),
and magenta (master/arch-).
> 9. There are these many members of the 'N' group.
Black, red, golden, and guardian nagas (and their associated
hatchlings).
> 10. These creatures carry white-handed shields.
Uruk-hai.
> 11. Kobolds are known for carrying these weapons.
Darts.
> 12. True or false: The Wizard of Yendor doesn't know how to use a
> weapon.
True - he has no weapon attack.
> 13. True or false: As a gnomish Healer, eating a Healer corpse is
> considered cannabalism.
False - healer corpse is considered human.
> 14. True or false: A mimic can ooze under doors.
True.
> 15. Tossing a gem to a non-aligned unicorn can change your luck in how
> many ways?
Seven - the range from -3 to +3 if the gem is properly identified (the
cases when the gem are not identified are from -1 to 1, which is
included).
> 16. A faded pall is the description for what type of item?
Elven cloak.
> 19. A hard hat is the description for what type of item?
Dwarvish iron helm.
> 20. True or false: Trying to genocide the 'A' group will have the same
> result as trying to genocide 'E'.
False - the A group is completely forbidden, but E genocides stalkers.
> 21. There are these many members in the 'V' group.
Vampires, vampire lords, and Vlad the Impaler.
> 22. When can you see the image of someone stalking you?
When you drink from a fountain and gain the see invisible intrinsic.
> 23. True or false: Humans can safely eat Quantum Mechanics, Stalkers,
> and Kops.
True, false (for the stunning effect), and true, in that order.
> 24. If you see a red ;, what creature(s) might it be?
Krakenxs and piranhas.
> 25. True or false: Gray Oozes can damage your armour.
True - they cause rust damage with their normal attack.



